# FPLBud codebase map

Fantasy Premier League assistant. A guest enters a public team ID and gets a next-gameweek plan. A signed-in user (Google via Supabase) saves a team, and a background agent writes plans for the next 1, 3 and 5 gameweeks.

Python is a uv workspace: `fplcore`, `api`, `ingest`. The UI is a separate pnpm app in `web/`. Domain logic lives in `fplcore`. `api` and `ingest` call it. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing metrics, the optimiser, the agent, or auth.

## Where to edit

| Change | Start here |
|---|---|
| Pages, layout, styling, browser behaviour | `web/` |
| HTTP routes, JWT checks, rate limits, request wiring | `api/src/api/` |
| FPL client, models, metrics, optimiser, agent, explanations, stats maths, DB access | `fplcore/src/fplcore/` |
| Scheduled fetch, upsert, metric recompute, queue drain | `ingest/src/ingest/run.py` and `.github/workflows/ingest.yml` |
| Tables and RLS | `db/schema.sql`, then a new file in `db/migrations/` |
| Python tests | `tests/` at the repo root |
| Frozen FPL API payloads | `samples/` |
| One-off DB scripts | `scripts/` |

## `fplcore` (`fplcore/src/fplcore/`)

- `client.py`, `models.py` — public FPL API and pydantic types
- `team_import.py` — squad, bank, free transfers, selling-price estimates, snapshots
- `metrics/` — per-player scores (`compute.py`) and projected points (`combine.py`)
- `optimise.py` — PuLP transfer, XI and captain solve
- `agent/` — queue (`queue.py`), run (`runner.py`), chip advice (`chips.py`)
- `explain/` — template text; the LLM explainer is optional and off by default
- `stats/` — market, insights, squad and season reports
- `rules.py` — transfer legality used by chat and checked against the optimiser
- `chat/` — assistant loop, events, prompt, guard. Import submodules directly
- `db/` — Postgres connection, `repos.py`, `stats_repo.py` and `chat_repo.py`
- `settings.py`, `constants.py`

## `api` (`api/src/api/`)

`main.py` mounts the routers and starts the in-process agent poll loop (`worker.py`). `auth.py` verifies the Supabase JWT. `services.py` orchestrates `fplcore`.

- `routers/public.py` — `GET /public/team/{entry_id}`
- `routers/suggestions.py` — `POST /suggestions` (guests are locked to horizon 1 and default weights)
- `routers/players.py`, `routers/stats.py`, `routers/meta.py`, `routers/health.py`
- `routers/me.py` — profile, team import, account delete
- `routers/agent.py` — rerun and run polling. Latest succeeded run comes from `fplcore.db.repos.latest_succeeded_run`
- `routers/chat.py` and `chat/` — SSE assistant. The stream authenticates with `chat_user` and does not hold `deps.db_conn`

## `web` (Next.js 16 App Router)

Read `web/AGENTS.md` before using Next.js APIs.

- `app/(site)/` — `/`, `/try/[entryId]`, `/dashboard` (plus `/squad`, `/plans`, `/insights`), `/chat`, `/settings`, `/onboarding`, `/how-it-works`
- `app/api/chat/stream/route.ts` — session proxy in front of the SSE route. `lib/chat.ts` parses the events
- `app/login`, `app/auth/callback` — Google sign-in
- `components/programme/` — shared editorial UI (pitch, plans, forms)
- `components/dashboard/` — signed-in dashboard and stats
- `lib/api.ts` — FastAPI client; `lib/server/` — server data and actions; `lib/supabase/` — session

```bash
uv run pytest -q
uv run --package api uvicorn api.main:app --reload --port 8000
uv run python -m ingest.run bootstrap
cd web && pnpm dev
```
